# UI, Accessibility, And Testing Rules

## UI

- The first screen should be the usable relationship graph, not a marketing landing page.
- Keep dense operational UI clear and restrained.
- Use the visual rules from `memory-bank/@game-design-document.md`.
- Avoid text overlap, button overflow, and panels that cover core graph controls.

## Accessibility

- Do not rely on color alone for relationship types; pair color with line style or labels.
- Respect reduced-motion preferences.
- Make important controls keyboard accessible.
- Provide readable labels for icon-only controls.

## Testing

- Use Vitest for schema, filter, collectible, and graph conversion logic.
- Use Playwright for at least one smoke test covering load, search, node selection, and detail panel update.
- Add tests when changing shared domain logic or user-facing interaction behavior.

